    "circle entries report more administrative and staff dysfunctional practices (unresponsiveness, nepotism/favoritism, hiring problems, inconsistent teacher quality, counseling/special‑education failures, allegations of misconduct and discriminatory discipline) than square entries": "Collects the many circle complaints about personnel, governance, and operational accountability (e.g., nepotism, protected tenured staff, lost paperwork, front‑office silence, IEP implementation gaps, gradebook/discipline bias) and is mutually exclusive from the academic/outcomes and extracurricular/community buckets because it concerns staff behavior and institutional process rather than program offerings or measurable student outcomes.",
    "circle entries report more pervasive student-safety problems, bullying, fights, racial harassment, sexual harassment, gang activity, and administrative minimization or nonresponse than square entries": "Captures circle reviews documenting peer‑violence and safety failures (frequent fights, bullying, sexual assault allegations, drugs/vaping, robbery rumors, identity‑based harassment) and the administration’s minimization or nonresponse, and is distinct from the staff‑dysfunction bucket because it centers on student‑to‑student harms and their supervision/response rather than hiring practices, favoritism, or special‑education/counseling operations."
}"]

["{
    "circle entries report more pervasive student-safety problems, bullying, fights, racial harassment, sexual harassment, gang activity, and administrative minimization or nonresponse than square entries": "This bucket isolates concrete safety-and-misconduct incidents and the school's failure-to-protect/minimize responses—a distinct domain (student safety and incident handling) that does not overlap with programmatic/college-prep claims or with personnel/governance dysfunction (other buckets).",
    "circle entries report more administrative and staff dysfunctional practices (unresponsiveness, nepotism/favoritism, hiring problems, inconsistent teacher quality, counseling/special‑education failures, allegations of misconduct and discriminatory discipline) than square entries": "This bucket groups personnel, governance and operational dysfunction (hiring, favoritism, counseling/SpEd failures, dishonest or discriminatory discipline) which is substantively different from safety incidents (bucket 1) and from program/offering or outcomes descriptions (the existing academic/extracurricular buckets).",
    "circle entries report stronger formal college‑preparatory programs, measurable academic outcomes, and advanced‑course/dual‑enrollment opportunities than square entries": "This bucket captures formal, measurable college-prep strength (outcome metrics, AP/IB/dualenrollment access and placement results) as an outcomes-and-program-strength axis distinct from the already-selected bucket about enumerated advanced-program types/partnerships (which documents program existence and partnerships) and distinct from safety or staff-dysfunction themes."
}"]

["{
    "circle entries report more pervasive student-safety problems, bullying, fights, racial harassment, sexual harassment, gang activity, and administrative minimization or nonresponse than square entries": "Groups reviews that document concrete on-campus safety incidents and a culture of student-on-student harm (and the school's failure to remedy them) — a discrete theme about safety and incident response that is not about staffing/HR dysfunction, curricular offerings, or community/extracurricular strengths.",
    "circle entries report more administrative and staff dysfunctional practices (unresponsiveness, nepotism/favoritism, hiring problems, inconsistent teacher quality, counseling/special‑education failures, allegations of misconduct and discriminatory discipline) than square entries": "Captures reviews centered on personnel, governance and service-delivery breakdowns (hiring, favoritism, counselor/IEP failures, unprofessional staff behavior) — a governance/HR/service-quality bucket that is distinct from student-safety incident reports and from programmatic/outcome descriptions.",
    "circle entries report stronger formal college‑preparatory programs, measurable academic outcomes, and advanced‑course/dual‑enrollment opportunities than square entries": "Isolates reviews that emphasize formal, measurable college-prep evidence (dual-credit enrollments, scholarship totals, SAT/ACT outcomes and documented placement results) — focused on outcome/credential metrics rather than the mere presence or breadth of advanced programs or extracurricular/community partnerships covered by the other selected buckets."
